{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED and PUSHED as Gerrit 1906, Change-Id Iadc2675a. Rebased onto origin/main d4acf9c373 first. apply_handlers.py 543 -> 544 (net +1); ADR 0099 294 -> 458 lines.\n\nTHE CUT: three lines became one. `entry = ctx.binding_store.all_bindings().get(local_id)` plus the isinstance guard plus `peer_state.note_rich_emit(entry, wire)` became `ctx.binding_store.note_rich_emit(local_id, wire) != peer_state.RICH_REEMIT_OBSERVE_AT`. The missing binding stays nonfatal because the operation returns None, deliberately distinct from 0, so one equality covers both the absent binding and the below-threshold case. Diff stayed tight to _observe_rich_reemit and its docstring; _rich_cutover_active untouched as required.\n\nFIFTH FALSE DOCUMENTED CLAIM OF THIS EPIC, and the one that had been actively load-bearing: the docstring justified mutation-through-query with \"binding_store.py sits at the module-size cap and cannot carry a narrower accessor\". Both halves were false - S2 T3 added the accessor, and that file is 554 lines. The pattern across all five is consistent: a workaround outlives the constraint that justified it, and the comment explaining the workaround is what keeps it alive. A test now asserts the phrase is gone, and it is mutation-verified.\n\nTHE CENSUS IS AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A BAN, AND IT IS PARSED RATHER THAN GREPPED. The reviewer's plan-review advisory asked how the census would distinguish a MUTATION through all_bindings() from a benign READ, which was the right question: four production readers legitimately iterate through it (binding_walk, reconcile_helpers, reconcile_check, _commands/bridge_repair), and I verified each by reading the call site - every write in those modules goes through a named facade method (set_baseline, merge_baseline, unbind). So the test records which callers may call it and why, and a NEW caller fails until someone classifies it in writing. It uses ast to find real Call nodes: a substring search matched four extra files that only DISCUSS all_bindings() in prose, and those are the files most likely to mention it and least likely to misuse it.\n\nADR 0099 FINALIZED. It described a plan; it now records what landed, and states which parts are behaviour rather than intention so weakening one is a behaviour change, not a plan revision. Realized classifier rules, tombstone authority versus explicit unretire, the intentional behaviour delta and its rollback, and the no-broad-staging prohibition are all in. The section that matters most records the invocation boundary AND why run_differs.py cannot host it, then instructs whoever next splits the capped reconcile.py to keep the call between the staleness gate and the first fetch, naming test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation as the oracle. RP-03 S5 is queued against that file, so the instruction has a known audience - also filed as insectile-modest-martin (d7b9-ac42-ad6f-4608).\n\nTWO ADR CLAIMS HAD GONE STALE UNDER RP-04 AND ARE CORRECTED. Section 9 said cutting the lifecycle config reads to a seam was \"still not RP-02's work\" and that both legacy-exception rows had been re-registered under binding_lifecycle.py. RP-04 C3g (toadyish-magic-arrowana) has since made that cut: _env_int is gone from all of src/, binding_lifecycle.py no longer references os, note_absent calls resolve_absent_retire_grace(), and the exceptions registry is drained to EMPTY so those rows no longer exist. Behaviour preserved - same variable, default 3, clamp to minimum 1. The companion claim that docs/env-vars.md records line numbers for those reads is void now the reads are gone; the general lesson is kept in one sentence because it bit three times in this epic. The implementer verified every one of these independently rather than trusting my summary.\n\nA HAZARD I CHECKED AND CLEARED rather than assumed: the set_flag fixture in the rich-reemit suite patches rebar.config.load_config, while RP-04 changed _rich_cutover_active to call compose_config(). I suspected the fixture had gone inert - which would have made the production oracles vacuous exactly where I needed them as the regression half - and probed it. compose_config() delegates to load_config internally, so the fixture is live and the oracles are meaningful. Worth recording because the real project config has rich_text_cutover = 'cloud', so the flag is ON by default and an inert fixture would NOT have shown up as a failure.\n\nHELD-OUT TDD: 36 oracles, of which the 29 pre-existing tests are the compatibility half and had to pass UNCHANGED - the cutover is required to be behaviour-preserving, so a change in the counter progression, the single read-back, the baseline route or the fail-open branches would be a regression rather than an improvement. The implementer saw 34; 2 discriminators were held outside the worktree and both passed unseen. Implementer: 1 attempt per part, and it verified it had touched no test file by hash.\n\nMUTATION: 3 of 4 killed - reverting to mutation-through-query, turning the equality threshold into a floor, and restoring the false accessor claim. The fourth SURVIVED and is a provably EQUIVALENT mutant, not an oracle gap: coercing the missing binding's None to 0 cannot be observed because RICH_REEMIT_OBSERVE_AT is 2, so a coerced 0 never equals it. I did NOT manufacture a test for it, applying the same judgement S2 T2 used for the unobservable env clamp - such a test could only assert implementation. It does surface a mild overstatement: the facade docstring says a 0 \"would trigger the caller's read-back for a binding that is not there\", which holds only if the threshold were ever lowered to 0 or 1. The None remains the right defensive choice; the hazard is latent, not present. Recorded rather than chased, since correcting it means editing binding_store.py, which is outside this task's declared impact.\n\nGATES: 3455 passed / 9 skipped across the reconciler unit tree, interfaces/store, reconciler integration, the docs-index and ADR-number suites and the comment-hygiene guard; lint clean, mypy 567, complexity new=0 increased=0, comment hygiene, config ownership, env registry unchanged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787156976713593001,"uuid":"c3462879-5dab-4018-9b88-9195904fb0ce"}